course: dictionary
lesson: 3072
title: Eden, a perfect place
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Eden, with a capital E, is the name of a place in the Bible story called the Garden of Eden. A proper noun is a name, and Eden is a proper noun when it names that garden.
explain: «Genesis 2 tells of the Garden of Eden, a beautiful garden where God put the first people to live and to work.» The clue words beautiful and garden tell you it was a lovely place. Eden is used this way in the story, so look at the words around it.
explain: Writers also borrow the name. «Writers call a lovely garden or island "an Eden".» Here Eden is a noun meaning any very beautiful, peaceful place, like a paradise. You can check by swapping in the meaning: "a peaceful paradise" should still make sense.
fact: Eden with a capital E is the name of the Garden of Eden in the Bible.
fact: «Eden» can mean a paradise: any very beautiful, peaceful place.
fact: In the Bible, Adam and Eve were placed in the Garden of Eden, the first man and woman.
fact: Eden was where the first people lived before they disobeyed and had to leave.
fact: The Eden Project is a famous garden in giant domes in Cornwall, and its name borrows the idea of a perfect garden.
exercise: «Genesis 2 tells of the Garden of Eden, a beautiful garden where God put the first people to live and to work.» Where did God put the first people? | In a big city | On a ship at sea | A cold, dark cave | *In the Garden of Eden
exercise: Sam says an Eden is a noisy city full of traffic. What does an Eden really mean? | A dark forest with no light | *Any very beautiful, peaceful place, like a paradise | A type of fruit | A busy, noisy city
exercise: «Adam and Eve are the first man and woman in the Bible.» Find and copy the name of a person in this sentence. | *Adam | first | woman | garden
test: «In Genesis 2 and 3 God places Adam and Eve, the first man and woman, in the Garden of Eden and lets them eat from every tree except one.» What were Adam and Eve allowed to eat from? | Nothing at all | *Every tree except one | Only the tree of the knowledge of good and evil | Only the fruit on the ground
test: «Writers call a lovely garden or island "an Eden".» Why might a writer call a holiday island "a little Eden"? | Because it is a school full of students | *Because it is a beautiful, peaceful place | Because it has a lot of traffic | Because it is cold, dark and empty
exam: The Eden Project is a famous garden in giant domes in Cornwall. Why might visitors say it is a little Eden? | Because it is a busy city with a lot of noise | *Because it is a beautiful, peaceful garden full of plants | Because it is a dark cave underground | Because it is grey, wet and dull
